  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef inference_symmetric_int8_quantization(x: list) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Implement Symmetric INT8 Quantization** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef inference_symmetric_int8_quantization(x: list) -> dict:\n    arr = np.array(x, dtype=float)\n    mv = np.max(np.abs(arr))\n    s = mv / 127.0 if mv > 0 else 1.0\n    return {'quantized': np.clip(np.round(arr / s), -128, 127).astype(int).tolist(), 'scale': round(float(s), 6)}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
